ack: node
is: Every cited line reads as the node says and the first review's three amendments are in it. One sentence is still off: 'This study read three definitions'. The study report read one of the three, substrate-phase.fk; the runtime's three homes and living-equation.fk come from the form-language and runtime-jit reports. The node holds with 'Three definitions were read' and a limit saying which report read which, as node 3.3.4.8 does for its own lines.
why: The study's reading list names substrate-phase.fk and neither the runtime nor living-equation.fk (study/r1/axioms-north-star.md:14-37), and its T16 says the definition lives in substrate-phase.fk (lines 597-605). The critic's spot-checks R4 and A8 give the other two to form-language and runtime-jit (study/r1/critic.md:215,225).
limit: On gas and nothing: substrate-phase.fk:18 glosses gas as 'diffuse — potential, barely instantiated', the old line 55 says the unreferenced 'returns to potential', and axiom 1 now calls nothing the shared potential field to which the unreferenced return (core-axioms.form:48). The word potential is the only bridge; no file read states the relation, so the node's sentence stands. At 9d7790856 itself the file already has no ice and no gas.
by: r3/close-ground-documents
at: 2026-11-24

